WEBVTT

00:33.950 --> 00:34.993
Oh.

00:35.785 --> 00:37.829
A dog shit dream.

00:59.476 --> 01:03.605
A KILLER PARADOX

01:10.820 --> 01:11.905
My goodness!

01:11.988 --> 01:14.324
How can you scare your mom,
sneaking around like that?

01:14.407 --> 01:16.409
What are you doing here?
You didn't mention…

01:16.493 --> 01:18.328
Well, since you're here,
go throw this away.

01:19.287 --> 01:22.290
Oh, did you come over to eat?
I don't have anything prepared.

01:22.373 --> 01:24.542
-Are you going somewhere?
-I'm going to church.

01:24.626 --> 01:27.337
Oh, speaking of which,
do you want to tag along?

01:27.420 --> 01:29.672
Oh, no, no.
Actually, I'd prefer to go alone.

01:29.756 --> 01:32.550
When Yeong comes back,
just order some takeout with her.

01:48.733 --> 01:50.026
Are you serious?

01:50.652 --> 01:53.279
Really? He actually said that to you?

01:53.822 --> 01:57.325
How could he say something like that
when he's the one that cheated?

01:57.408 --> 01:59.744
You should've pulled out all his hair
and humiliated him.

01:59.828 --> 02:01.246
You can't just let him be.

02:01.746 --> 02:02.831
You have to dump him.

02:03.331 --> 02:05.625
-That asshole deserves a good pruning.
-Excuse me.

02:06.126 --> 02:07.919
-Why tell me this now?
-Excuse me.

02:08.002 --> 02:09.671
Sorry, one sec. Customer.

02:09.754 --> 02:10.630
Yeah?

02:10.713 --> 02:12.006
What's the price?

02:12.090 --> 02:13.716
The small ones are 30,000 won,

02:13.800 --> 02:16.052
the big ones 50,000,
the medium ones 40,000.

02:16.136 --> 02:18.346
-Pots, 6,000. Tell me when you decide.
-Which is small?

02:18.429 --> 02:19.430
-What?
-I mean…

02:19.514 --> 02:20.807
Three years?

02:21.724 --> 02:23.643
Oh! Oh, my goodness.

02:24.227 --> 02:27.021
How could he do this
behind your back for three years?

02:27.772 --> 02:29.232
You're an idiot.

02:29.315 --> 02:31.651
How can you not notice
that for three years?

02:31.734 --> 02:34.404
Oh, welcome.

02:34.487 --> 02:36.197
Hey, uh, do you have one of those

02:37.240 --> 02:38.449
juice gift sets?

02:38.533 --> 02:39.701
The box with handles?

02:39.784 --> 02:42.036
PREMIUM JUICE SET

02:43.079 --> 02:45.957
Sir, could you get me a new one?
This one is really dusty.

02:51.713 --> 02:53.923
Yeah, I'll go grab a new one.

02:55.300 --> 02:56.551
Picky bastard.

03:49.938 --> 03:52.273
You could've put the trash in the bin.

03:53.399 --> 03:56.277
Next time you come,
at least buy some flowers.

03:56.361 --> 03:57.403
He's your dad.

03:58.488 --> 04:00.240
It's not like you come every day.

04:00.782 --> 04:02.659
You only get one father.

04:02.742 --> 04:06.246
-For goodness' sake.
-Father never cared for flowers. Hmm?

04:06.746 --> 04:09.749
The only one he liked was
the hibiscus on his rank insignia.

04:20.218 --> 04:21.344
I'm gonna go.

04:23.471 --> 04:25.348
Why even bother coming?

04:27.809 --> 04:29.435
Have you been losing weight?

04:30.520 --> 04:33.481
Hey. Have you been skipping school
and drinking again?

04:33.982 --> 04:35.066
What are you saying?

04:35.942 --> 04:39.320
Listen, you really can't slack off
on any of your studies right now.

04:39.404 --> 04:41.322
Not because of your working holiday.

04:41.406 --> 04:45.535
You were just like this before too.
Up until you joined the army, that is.

04:45.618 --> 04:48.579
Oh, are you going to college
just to get kicked out? Huh?

04:48.663 --> 04:49.622
-Unbelie--
-Hello.

04:49.706 --> 04:52.625
Oh, hi, hi, hi!
Hello. Hi. Good to see you.

04:52.709 --> 04:54.877
I don't even want to think
about those days.

04:54.961 --> 04:57.130
You're not that young anymore.
You're grown.

04:57.213 --> 04:58.965
-Don't be so--
-It's not what you think.

04:59.465 --> 05:02.302
And I can always retake the classes
and get the credits.

05:02.844 --> 05:05.513
Do you think I don't know that
because I didn't go to college?

05:05.596 --> 05:07.598
Hey! If you're going to retake classes,

05:07.682 --> 05:10.560
that costs double the normal amount,
doesn't it?

05:10.643 --> 05:12.770
Yeah. If you get two academic
probations, you're out.

05:12.854 --> 05:14.731
-Oh! Deacon Kim.
-Right? And you are…

05:15.523 --> 05:17.025
Oh, hi. Hello!

05:17.108 --> 05:19.944
-You look so lovely!
-Oh, I do? Ah!

05:20.028 --> 05:22.488
-Aah!
-Yeah, thank you. So do you.

05:22.572 --> 05:25.158
And this must be Tang.

05:25.241 --> 05:26.576
You should say hello.

05:26.659 --> 05:28.202
Oh gosh. He's tall.

05:28.703 --> 05:30.955
And what about Yeong's wedding?
It's tough, right?

05:31.039 --> 05:34.792
Oh, well, I've taken care of the stuff
that was complicated for her already.

05:34.876 --> 05:38.796
I'm just getting the two of them a small
apartment, so they can take it easy.

05:38.880 --> 05:41.758
This one's all grown up, too,
and he's going abroad soon.

05:41.841 --> 05:43.217
-Wow. Really?
-Yeah.

05:43.301 --> 05:45.636
-Where?
-Australia, in fact. Honey, come on!

05:45.720 --> 05:47.221
That's great news!

05:47.305 --> 05:48.765
-Hello!
-Oh, hello.

05:48.848 --> 05:52.226
Because Jesus Christ was crucified
on the cross, we are now saved…

05:52.310 --> 05:57.607
Listen, when your father retires, we can
live off his pension, as small as it is.

05:57.690 --> 06:00.568
So don't worry. Just go and work hard.

06:00.651 --> 06:02.820
…we know what it is to do good…

06:02.904 --> 06:08.117
We can't afford to help you study abroad
like some other parents would be able to.

06:08.785 --> 06:10.912
But we won't burden our kids.

06:14.165 --> 06:15.208
Understand?

06:17.126 --> 06:18.544
Hold onto this.

06:18.628 --> 06:19.504
LOTTERY TICKET

06:19.587 --> 06:21.255
-Don't ever smoke marijuana.
-Jeez.

06:22.507 --> 06:24.258
And wear condoms. Stay safe.

06:24.342 --> 06:25.968
-All right?
-All right.

06:26.052 --> 06:28.012
He is the salt of the earth.

06:28.096 --> 06:30.807
Ah! Listen, did you hear about the guy
who was killed

06:30.890 --> 06:33.393
near the convenience store
that you work at?

06:33.476 --> 06:35.269
…life of grace and mercy…

06:35.353 --> 06:38.398
Oh, honestly, he had it coming.

06:38.481 --> 06:41.025
It was God's retribution, surely.

06:41.609 --> 06:44.946
Oh, how could such a thing happen?
Goodness.

06:53.162 --> 06:55.248
Why are you all standin' around?

06:55.331 --> 06:58.668
We're getting heat
for not catching Yeo Bu-il before he died.

06:58.751 --> 07:03.005
The bosses are givin' us crap about
arrest numbers goin' down for cold cases.

07:03.506 --> 07:06.968
And the chief called up the captain,
so we're all walkin' on thin ice.

07:07.051 --> 07:10.930
-Why is everyone standing around?
-Well, we're gettin' some heat for, uh…

07:13.975 --> 07:17.311
You jerk. Why are you buyin' us coffee
when you get paid peanuts?

07:17.395 --> 07:20.189
-Seriously. Come on…
-It's fine, sir. Have some. No?

07:20.773 --> 07:22.066
Have some coffee, here.

07:22.150 --> 07:24.068
-Great work, everyone.
-Ah. Thank you.

07:24.152 --> 07:25.778
There's one for everybody.

07:25.862 --> 07:27.822
-Here you go. Did you all get one?
-Hey.

07:27.905 --> 07:29.198
-Come here…
-Sir?

07:29.282 --> 07:31.451
You keep goin' back to see that cute girl.

07:31.951 --> 07:33.786
Is she cute? I hadn't noticed.

07:33.870 --> 07:37.248
-We'll sing at your wedding.
-You got it wrong. It's not like that.

07:37.331 --> 07:38.875
-What are you naming your kid?
-Uh, sir.

07:38.958 --> 07:40.293
-Sir.
-Hello, sir.

07:40.376 --> 07:41.878
-Oh.
-Hello, sir.

07:42.545 --> 07:44.172
You all heard, huh?

07:44.672 --> 07:45.590
Sir…

07:47.884 --> 07:49.343
-Thanks.
-Yeah.

07:49.427 --> 07:51.053
Get it together, everyone.

07:51.846 --> 07:53.973
Don't wait until next month
to get started.

07:54.056 --> 07:55.850
Start getting ready now.

07:55.933 --> 07:59.770
Use this opportunity,
and get those awards and promotions, huh?

07:59.854 --> 08:01.105
-Yes, sir.
-Yep.

08:01.189 --> 08:02.732
Okay, then get to work.

08:02.815 --> 08:03.983
-Sir.
-Yes, sir.

08:04.901 --> 08:06.777
-Hey. Detective Jang.
-Yeah?

08:07.820 --> 08:10.281
Look, you need to stop
fixating on that guy.

08:10.364 --> 08:12.492
-Don't try to be a lone wolf.
-I'm not fixating.

08:12.575 --> 08:13.951
-What's that about?
-Come on.

08:14.035 --> 08:17.163
-I got it.
-Well, there was a guy we couldn't catch.

08:17.246 --> 08:18.372
Who was he?

08:18.998 --> 08:20.500
A cop, just like you.

08:21.501 --> 08:24.921
A cop? A cop on the run? Whoa.

08:25.004 --> 08:26.756
-That's messed up.
-Eh, well.

08:26.839 --> 08:30.468
Every detective has that one perp
they want to catch more than anything.

08:30.551 --> 08:32.345
-Ahem. Detective An.
-Yes, sir.

08:32.428 --> 08:34.639
We have a simple saying.

08:34.722 --> 08:39.435
Being a detective here is like
riding on top of a really thin line.

08:39.519 --> 08:40.770
Mm.

08:40.853 --> 08:43.981
It's fine if you can
keep your balance on it.

08:44.732 --> 08:46.567
But if you were to slip,

08:46.651 --> 08:49.278
you go back to an average citizen.

08:49.362 --> 08:51.364
-Mm-hmm.
-If you're lucky.

08:51.447 --> 08:53.574
But if you fall on the other side,
that means prison.

08:54.534 --> 08:56.285
If you don't wanna go to prison,

08:56.953 --> 08:58.079
you run away.

08:59.288 --> 09:00.915
That's how it goes in this life.

09:01.916 --> 09:02.959
Here you go.

09:04.877 --> 09:07.213
Feel free to reach out
if you have any issues.

09:10.675 --> 09:11.592
You're all set.

09:12.426 --> 09:13.427
Thank you.

09:18.933 --> 09:20.142
Have a good day.

09:26.774 --> 09:27.817
Have a good day.

09:30.570 --> 09:31.779
Have a good day.

09:34.574 --> 09:35.700
Have a good day.

09:38.953 --> 09:40.162
What are you doing?

09:41.289 --> 09:42.123
Oh.

09:42.999 --> 09:45.501
It's the… The door seems misaligned.

09:47.003 --> 09:48.629
Jeez.

09:48.713 --> 09:50.673
Don't you just hate that sound?

09:51.924 --> 09:53.884
All that "Have a good day!
Have a good day!"

09:53.968 --> 09:55.636
whenever anyone comes or goes.

09:56.262 --> 09:58.723
It's like it'll kill us
if we don't have a good day.

10:00.433 --> 10:02.935
If that thing breaks,
you'll know the reason.

10:04.270 --> 10:06.814
The manager is psycho
for keeping that thing.

10:09.066 --> 10:10.151
Huh?

10:10.234 --> 10:12.903
-Yeah, the… the manager totally is--
-Yes! Time to go.

10:22.580 --> 10:23.623
Have a good day.

10:28.961 --> 10:29.962
Shit.

10:31.839 --> 10:32.798
Hello.

10:33.633 --> 10:35.301
Let me know if you need anything.

10:35.801 --> 10:37.845
Can I get a pack of Raison French?

10:37.928 --> 10:39.013
Raison…

10:48.898 --> 10:50.608
Hmm. Mm!

10:53.653 --> 10:54.820
Oh, also,

10:56.155 --> 10:57.114
two million won.

10:58.491 --> 10:59.617
What?

10:59.700 --> 11:02.411
You need to give me two million won.

11:03.037 --> 11:05.164
Hmm? In cash, that is.

11:07.750 --> 11:08.793
Um…

11:09.543 --> 11:10.544
I don't understand.

11:14.548 --> 11:16.133
You look stunned!

11:18.219 --> 11:19.428
You know me, don't you?

11:22.848 --> 11:23.933
Huh?

11:25.017 --> 11:26.018
You should.

11:28.229 --> 11:29.522
Do you know me?

11:31.065 --> 11:33.484
Ugh, the fuck is wrong with everyone?

11:34.819 --> 11:37.113
What they see is all they care about.

11:37.196 --> 11:38.155
Look.

11:40.825 --> 11:41.659
These.

11:42.827 --> 11:45.329
You think I'm blind, don't you, huh?

11:48.165 --> 11:50.501
But I can still see a bit, you know.

11:58.926 --> 12:00.302
So how was it? Huh?

12:00.803 --> 12:02.221
To murder that guy.

12:04.974 --> 12:07.059
Aah!

12:07.143 --> 12:08.978
Ah, never mind that. Uh…

12:09.061 --> 12:12.231
How much do you make
from working here, then? Huh?

12:12.314 --> 12:13.399
Do you make anything?

12:16.652 --> 12:19.947
It's like I'm talkin'
to a fuckin' brick wall.

12:20.948 --> 12:22.450
Oh!

12:22.533 --> 12:26.620
Hmm. It must be so easy to dox you
with such a unique name.

12:27.997 --> 12:29.039
Anyway…

12:29.707 --> 12:32.084
Uh, think about it, okay?

12:32.168 --> 12:33.544
Two million.

12:34.128 --> 12:35.463
Have a good day.

12:39.383 --> 12:41.260
Oh, by the way,

12:42.845 --> 12:44.889
I'm not seeing any hammers, huh?

12:46.599 --> 12:49.268
Anyway, please have it ready by tomorrow.

12:52.062 --> 12:53.105
Have a good day.

12:53.189 --> 12:55.065
Have a good day.
Have a good day.

12:55.149 --> 12:57.443
Have a good day. Have a good day…

13:13.501 --> 13:15.002
-Bye!
-See you!

13:17.004 --> 13:19.131
-I'm wearing tiger boxers today.
-Jesus.

13:19.215 --> 13:21.175
-With a giant tiger face.
-So what? I'm busy.

13:21.258 --> 13:23.302
Besides, I have to study for that test.

13:23.385 --> 13:25.888
-Where are you going to study?
-Someplace quiet.

13:25.971 --> 13:29.767
-Someplace quiet?
-Hey, listen. Tang called me earlier.

13:29.850 --> 13:32.853
-What'd he say?
-He asked if he could borrow some cash.

13:33.395 --> 13:35.481
That bastard must have gone crazy.

13:35.564 --> 13:37.566
He texted me the same exact thing.

13:37.650 --> 13:39.443
-It's so weird.
-Yeah.

13:40.110 --> 13:43.405
-Should the three of us talk about it?
-With Tang?

13:44.198 --> 13:45.407
With the tiger.

13:49.119 --> 13:51.747
Fucking shit!

13:52.540 --> 13:56.085
I've never seen
anyone ask for a refund for a phone.

13:58.838 --> 14:00.965
I mean, it's not like
the phone has issues.

14:01.966 --> 14:05.594
You took the screen protector off too.
There's nothing I can do for you.

14:06.804 --> 14:09.056
You can pay
for the phone in full

14:09.139 --> 14:11.475
and resell it as used to somebody else.

14:12.685 --> 14:15.563
People do it all the time.
That's all I can suggest.

14:16.355 --> 14:18.107
PART-TIME MARKET

14:19.733 --> 14:20.901
BALANCE: 192,370 WON

14:25.072 --> 14:26.615
SHORT-TERM JOBS

14:26.699 --> 14:29.368
SAME-DAY PAY JOBS

14:33.998 --> 14:34.957
Hey, sir.

14:37.376 --> 14:39.044
Why are you here at this hour?

14:39.128 --> 14:40.129
Well…

14:40.921 --> 14:43.465
I, uh, forgot to tell you
something yesterday.

14:44.508 --> 14:46.010
Go ahead. What is it, hmm?

14:46.093 --> 14:47.887
-You quitting?
-Huh?

14:47.970 --> 14:50.931
-Uh, no, that's not it.
-What is it, then?

14:51.432 --> 14:54.560
Uh… I have a situation.

14:55.769 --> 14:58.105
I was wondering
if you could pay me in advance.

14:58.188 --> 14:59.982
-For the whole month.
-Oh, gosh.

15:00.858 --> 15:04.486
Hey, do you remember the guy
who worked all my overnights last year?

15:04.570 --> 15:07.281
Oh? Remember what happened
after I paid him in advance?

15:07.364 --> 15:09.700
He gambled all the money away
and disappeared.

15:10.200 --> 15:12.036
It was a complete nightmare to deal with.

15:12.119 --> 15:14.371
I spent six months
trying to catch that guy.

15:14.872 --> 15:17.333
I've never paid anyone
in advance ever since then.

15:17.416 --> 15:18.709
You get it, huh?

15:18.792 --> 15:23.505
-I'm being honest with you without--
-Yeah, I… I understand. I really do.

15:24.048 --> 15:26.383
-But that's not me.
-Come on.

15:27.343 --> 15:28.844
You know how I work.

15:28.928 --> 15:31.972
No means no, huh? It's not happening.

15:33.515 --> 15:34.767
PART-TIME PAY: 961,000 WON

15:37.311 --> 15:39.730
BALANCE: 1,453,370 WON
KANG MI-YEONG SENT: 150,000 WON

15:39.813 --> 15:40.689
GYEONG-HWAN

15:43.943 --> 15:44.944
LEE TANG

15:47.571 --> 15:48.697
He must be losing it.

15:52.034 --> 15:53.786
BUSINESS STATISTICS MIDTERM

15:54.370 --> 15:56.205
HOUSING SUBSCRIPTION SAVINGS ACCOUNT

15:57.498 --> 15:58.415
BALANCE: 1,700,000 WON

15:58.499 --> 16:02.044
If you're going to keep coming
home to eat, why don't you move back in?

16:02.127 --> 16:05.005
Do you know how expensive
your rent is? Hmm?

16:05.089 --> 16:07.049
It's not like the school is that far.

16:07.132 --> 16:08.801
You keep going back and forth…

16:10.219 --> 16:12.012
What the… Tang!

16:14.682 --> 16:17.309
The longer you have this type of account,
the better it is.

16:17.393 --> 16:18.894
That's why I wouldn't cancel this.

16:18.978 --> 16:21.146
-When you try to buy a house later--
-Just…

16:22.189 --> 16:24.358
Just… Please. Just do it.

16:25.359 --> 16:26.360
Mm.

16:28.153 --> 16:29.571
Do you want 50,000 won bills?

16:29.655 --> 16:31.115
Uh, 10,000 won bills, please.

16:33.575 --> 16:34.660
Okay, then.

16:39.957 --> 16:41.375
Hey, you're early.

16:43.794 --> 16:44.670
END OF SHIFT

16:44.753 --> 16:46.130
Yes! Time to go home.

16:46.922 --> 16:48.007
Have a good one.

16:48.674 --> 16:49.675
Bye.

16:57.808 --> 16:58.892
Hi, welcome.

17:12.406 --> 17:13.282
GYEONG-HWAN

17:13.365 --> 17:14.283
Not now.

17:23.709 --> 17:25.210
MI-YEONG

17:31.925 --> 17:32.968
What the…

17:38.807 --> 17:39.975
What the heck?

17:40.059 --> 17:41.226
Jeez.

17:43.312 --> 17:46.065
Hello, sir. What are you doing?

17:46.148 --> 17:47.649
It's not making the sound.

17:48.150 --> 17:49.777
-Damn it.
-I wonder why.

17:51.070 --> 17:53.614
What are you doing with that bag?
You're working.

17:54.907 --> 17:57.785
Ah, I see. You getting ready to leave?
It's way too early.

17:57.868 --> 17:59.036
No.

18:00.120 --> 18:02.122
You're not gambling
with that money I gave you?

18:02.206 --> 18:04.541
-What's in there?
-What? Oh, no way.

18:05.250 --> 18:06.835
-Better not.
-Okay.

18:06.919 --> 18:08.796
-You're early today.
-Listen.

18:09.296 --> 18:12.174
I saw this weird woman
on my way over here.

18:12.716 --> 18:15.052
She creeped me out.
She's blind, I thought.

18:15.719 --> 18:17.805
Only it felt like she was staring.

18:17.888 --> 18:21.850
And she was just standing there all alone,
her head turning to the side and back.

18:21.934 --> 18:23.685
So fucking creepy.

18:25.145 --> 18:26.188
Hey!

18:53.173 --> 18:57.678
HOUSE WITH BLUE DOORS
BY THE YONGUN INTERSECTION

19:05.435 --> 19:08.689
CASE REPORT: BLUNT WEAPON ASSAULT
ON POLICE OFFICER, 2004, UNSOLVED

19:14.403 --> 19:15.320
Nan-gam.

19:17.281 --> 19:18.198
Yeah.

19:18.699 --> 19:20.284
Just focus on your life.

19:20.951 --> 19:22.911
Stop trying to get this guy.

19:22.995 --> 19:25.873
Stop trying to get vengeance
for what happened to your father.

19:25.956 --> 19:27.833
-It won't do you any good to obsess--
-Vengeance?

19:27.916 --> 19:30.794
Why would I try to avenge my father?
I'm not some teenager.

19:30.878 --> 19:33.046
All right, you disrespectful son of a--

19:33.130 --> 19:35.465
You wanted us to catch
guys with suspended charges.

19:35.549 --> 19:37.843
-So I'm reviewing these to get promoted.
-You punk.

19:37.926 --> 19:41.680
Just 'cause I've known you since you were
a kid, doesn't mean you can talk back…

19:43.682 --> 19:44.725
Hah!

19:44.808 --> 19:47.728
Ah, jeez. You've gotten
so soft in your golden years.

19:47.811 --> 19:50.480
-You little…
-I don't even wanna dodge that.

19:51.356 --> 19:52.399
Hello, sir.

19:53.400 --> 19:55.694
Hey. Please make sure you eat.

19:56.195 --> 19:58.405
And this clock is dead, by the way.

19:58.989 --> 20:00.199
See you later, sir.

20:10.709 --> 20:13.170
-You excited?
-I don't know.

20:13.253 --> 20:15.672
They don't look like they're cut out
for this sort of training.

20:16.798 --> 20:18.383
Did I keep you waiting?

20:21.220 --> 20:22.512
Hey!

20:22.596 --> 20:25.182
You can change the channel
if you really want.

20:26.600 --> 20:30.187
That's actually the only show I watch.
You know why?

20:32.022 --> 20:35.651
I watch it because dogs can't lie.

20:35.734 --> 20:39.446
Individuals,
on the other hand, I just…

20:39.529 --> 20:40.405
Ugh.

20:40.906 --> 20:42.449
He bared his teeth and barked.

20:42.532 --> 20:43.784
Then he pounced.

20:43.867 --> 20:44.826
So, uh…

20:45.661 --> 20:46.912
How was it, huh?

20:46.995 --> 20:48.705
For all animal lovers…

20:48.789 --> 20:50.958
You seemed a bit nervous.

20:52.709 --> 20:53.543
Here you go.

20:54.461 --> 20:56.213
That's my only cup in the house.

20:56.296 --> 20:59.007
It's expensive coffee, though,
so it should taste good.

21:00.717 --> 21:03.428
I've just been watching you to…

21:04.054 --> 21:06.974
to find out if you're
a person I can trust or not.

21:09.810 --> 21:11.311
Have you noticed? Huh?

21:11.812 --> 21:12.980
Look!

21:13.730 --> 21:16.733
I've been carrying on
a conversation all alone here. Huh?

21:18.527 --> 21:20.862
If you keep acting like this,
like you're mute,

21:20.946 --> 21:23.240
how do you think that makes me feel?

21:25.742 --> 21:26.702
Then again,

21:27.327 --> 21:28.578
I guess that's fair.

21:28.662 --> 21:31.123
I was acting like I couldn't see.

21:33.750 --> 21:35.043
Seriously, though,

21:35.544 --> 21:38.422
I was genuinely shocked that night.

21:39.214 --> 21:41.091
Just think about it, huh?

21:41.883 --> 21:45.929
I take night walks because I hate people,
and then I saw one dead.

21:47.472 --> 21:48.932
Then, and

21:49.683 --> 21:51.685
once again when I watched the news.

21:51.768 --> 21:52.769
Hmm.

21:53.270 --> 21:54.855
By the way, uh…

21:56.732 --> 21:58.734
did you kill the other guy too?

22:01.445 --> 22:02.612
N-no.

22:03.947 --> 22:05.032
I-I didn't.

22:05.741 --> 22:06.658
Huh.

22:07.617 --> 22:09.661
Now you speak.

22:10.996 --> 22:13.582
That's what I thought.

22:23.175 --> 22:24.217
Hmm.

22:28.597 --> 22:30.307
Show me the cash, huh?

22:34.770 --> 22:35.729
Ah.

22:37.230 --> 22:40.025
Ah. Two million. Well done.

22:42.027 --> 22:44.696
-Could you stack them up for me again?
-Okay.

22:46.406 --> 22:50.702
So, you're gonna
keep quiet about it, right?

22:50.786 --> 22:53.455
Hmm, sure will. Mm.

22:56.958 --> 23:01.004
So, um, I give you this,
and we have a deal then, right?

23:01.088 --> 23:03.715
Yeah, yeah, of course.

23:04.633 --> 23:07.344
Oh, I'm sure you remember,

23:07.427 --> 23:09.012
but it's every month, okay?

23:09.638 --> 23:10.764
Two million.

23:12.349 --> 23:13.266
Huh?

23:14.184 --> 23:17.604
-Wait. You never said that.
-Sure I did.

23:18.438 --> 23:20.524
I mean, isn't it obvious?

23:20.607 --> 23:23.151
Don't you have any common sense?

23:23.652 --> 23:25.028
For fuck's sake.

23:26.905 --> 23:28.365
I mean, are you crazy?

23:29.366 --> 23:30.242
What?

23:30.867 --> 23:32.661
I'm asking if you're crazy.

23:32.744 --> 23:35.580
Oh, come on, man.
You're making me an accomplice here.

23:41.545 --> 23:44.798
Who would do something
this dangerous for two million?

23:46.049 --> 23:46.967
Huh?

23:48.176 --> 23:50.053
Pay me at the end of every month.

23:50.137 --> 23:52.264
Actually, your payday works fine for me.

23:52.347 --> 23:54.182
We can figure out the details later.

23:56.435 --> 23:59.312
Oh, and bring 50,000 won bills next time.

24:04.359 --> 24:07.988
Oh!
My dog Rex just had to bring this home,

24:08.071 --> 24:11.241
when I was fucking annoyed already
because of the rain!

24:11.741 --> 24:12.617
Aww.

24:12.701 --> 24:15.120
That's just how Rex is.

24:15.620 --> 24:17.706
He's always so curious.

24:17.789 --> 24:21.001
He's always bringing stuff home
and wandering off somewhere.

24:21.084 --> 24:22.127
Huh!

24:24.921 --> 24:27.716
That's why he couldn't
make it as a seeing-eye dog.

24:27.799 --> 24:30.552
They said I wasn't blind
enough to apply for one anyway.

24:30.635 --> 24:33.430
So, we're like this little, uh, shitty…

24:35.432 --> 24:37.058
…pair, or somethin'.

24:38.185 --> 24:40.145
Duet? Oh!

24:40.228 --> 24:41.897
Look at us! A trio now!

24:41.980 --> 24:44.065
What do you say?

24:48.778 --> 24:50.489
That was just a joke.

24:51.031 --> 24:52.032
You should laugh.

24:52.949 --> 24:53.950
Oh!

24:56.453 --> 24:57.871
Listen.

24:59.873 --> 25:01.458
Folks get angry…

25:03.335 --> 25:05.921
when they stop getting paid, don't they?

25:07.422 --> 25:11.426
When that happens, well…
what would you do, huh?

25:12.969 --> 25:14.846
You'd go and speak to your boss.

25:16.139 --> 25:19.184
But then, what's the point, really?

25:19.267 --> 25:22.979
It's better to report your boss
to the Labor Administration.

25:24.648 --> 25:29.277
Only, for me, it would be the police,
not the Labor Administration.

25:29.361 --> 25:30.529
Oh!

25:31.863 --> 25:33.615
I'll give you two million won.

25:35.242 --> 25:36.243
But I'm taking this.

25:38.745 --> 25:40.872
Lee Tang, class of 2024 at Usang.

25:40.956 --> 25:43.500
I mean, it's a shithole,
but it's not jail.

25:44.501 --> 25:47.087
What, do you wanna ruin
your sweet sister's wedding?

25:47.629 --> 25:48.713
Oh, and what was it?

25:48.797 --> 25:52.092
Oh yeah. Your mom goes
to Daeseok Church, doesn't she, though?

25:52.175 --> 25:53.301
Oh.

25:54.177 --> 25:58.765
Well, then, I guess she won't be able
to go to that church anymore.

26:13.238 --> 26:14.531
Oh…

26:20.579 --> 26:21.538
Honey.

26:22.998 --> 26:24.833
I'm talking to you, huh?

26:26.126 --> 26:28.920
Do you think that taking that
changes things?

26:30.046 --> 26:31.548
No, it will make things worse.

26:32.424 --> 26:34.801
What's the word? Oh, forensic science. Oh!

26:35.552 --> 26:38.138
Forensic science is so thorough nowadays.

26:39.264 --> 26:42.434
I know that your DNA is
all over my house already.

26:43.518 --> 26:46.313
You know that if I testify
and the cops look your way,

26:47.147 --> 26:49.649
they'll turn your house
upside down in a second.

26:50.775 --> 26:53.153
I mean, then, it'll be game over in days.

26:54.029 --> 26:56.990
I know a thing or two about this.
Involuntary manslaughter.

26:57.073 --> 27:00.744
Even if that's the only charge,
you'll get put away for 15 years.

27:00.827 --> 27:03.163
And once you get out,
you'll be an ex-convict.

27:03.246 --> 27:05.165
So what would you do then, huh?

27:06.124 --> 27:08.209
Listen, I only want to help.

27:08.293 --> 27:09.919
I'll help you not get caught.

27:12.339 --> 27:13.506
Do you want that?

27:14.716 --> 27:15.800
Or not?

27:17.719 --> 27:19.679
And if you choose to be good,

27:20.722 --> 27:22.015
I'll give you a deal.

27:23.224 --> 27:26.186
You won't have to go to jail
or become an ex-con.

27:26.269 --> 27:28.980
And didn't you say
you wanted to go to Australia? Huh?

27:30.273 --> 27:33.818
If you keep the payments coming,
I'll let you visit, okay? Hmm?

27:36.112 --> 27:37.447
Do you want that?

27:38.531 --> 27:39.574
Beg, then.

27:43.370 --> 27:44.287
Help me.

27:45.205 --> 27:46.581
Say it nicely.

27:48.792 --> 27:49.918
Please help me.

27:54.047 --> 27:55.090
Good dog.

27:57.008 --> 27:58.051
Hmm?

28:11.314 --> 28:13.108
Come here!

28:35.130 --> 28:36.089
Huh.

28:37.215 --> 28:39.467
Shit, I must have misjudged you.

30:19.150 --> 30:21.152
Come on, let's go.

30:21.903 --> 30:23.696
All right. Good boy.

30:26.282 --> 30:27.116
Let's go.

30:27.200 --> 30:29.327
This isn't our house.

30:29.828 --> 30:30.870
Come on.

31:01.651 --> 31:02.735
What the…

31:10.577 --> 31:14.789
So she hasn't been taking the milk inside,
so you looked over the fence.

31:14.873 --> 31:19.252
And have you ever run into her
or ever seen her face before or anything?

31:19.919 --> 31:22.130
-Huh?
-I'm asking if you knew her.

31:22.213 --> 31:24.507
-Or if you've ever spoken with her before.
-Oh. No.

31:24.591 --> 31:26.843
So you don't know her. Okay, I got it.

31:27.969 --> 31:30.096
I might be getting in touch
with you later.

31:30.680 --> 31:32.265
-Oh.
-Here, take my card.

31:32.348 --> 31:34.475
I need you to text me
at this number today.

31:34.559 --> 31:36.269
-Oh, okay.
-Okay. You can go now.

31:36.352 --> 31:37.562
-Uh…
-Yes, you can go.

31:37.645 --> 31:39.272
-Okay! Thank you.
-Thanks for your time.

31:42.984 --> 31:44.235
Oh, hi.

31:44.319 --> 31:46.112
-We finished inside.
-All right. Thank you.

31:46.195 --> 31:47.363
-Have a good one.
-Thanks.

31:47.447 --> 31:48.740
-Bye, thank you.
-Bye. Bye.

31:50.074 --> 31:52.702
So. Did you remember to check his alibi?

31:53.870 --> 31:57.707
Uh, well, he delivered her milk here, and…

31:58.207 --> 31:59.626
-He looked over--
-Go after him, now.

31:59.709 --> 32:01.210
Yes, sir. I'm sorry.

32:01.294 --> 32:03.755
Scuse me.
I just have a few more questions.

32:04.339 --> 32:06.674
Man, what's with this neighborhood
these days?

32:07.967 --> 32:10.553
In my 20 years here,
never seen anything like this.

32:10.637 --> 32:13.181
Exactly. Just what the hell is all this?

32:14.390 --> 32:15.391
Shit…

32:16.309 --> 32:18.019
Hey, looks like revenge.

32:18.102 --> 32:20.480
We'll have to see the autopsy results.

32:20.563 --> 32:22.523
But just look at how damaged the body is.

32:23.149 --> 32:24.359
-Hmm?
-Sit.

32:24.442 --> 32:27.320
Is the dog also blind? Can't he tell
what's food and what isn't?

32:27.403 --> 32:28.780
Gosh, would you look at that?

32:28.863 --> 32:30.865
I guess
she wasn't completely blind.

32:31.532 --> 32:32.617
Down. Down.

32:32.700 --> 32:34.786
-Well, it might be for her family.
-Down!

32:34.869 --> 32:35.995
She lives alone.

32:36.079 --> 32:37.163
Hey!

32:37.246 --> 32:38.873
Maybe she just listened to it.

32:38.957 --> 32:40.416
Oh! This is 8K!

32:40.500 --> 32:42.585
-Hey, what's that idiot doing?
-What?

32:42.669 --> 32:44.128
It's really expensive!

32:44.212 --> 32:45.964
-Stop it, all right?
-Ugh, that idiot.

32:46.047 --> 32:48.967
-Come here.
-Put a leash on the dog! Moron!

32:49.050 --> 32:52.637
Jeez! Why are you being so loud?
Quiet down. I'll go down.

32:52.720 --> 32:54.681
Jeez, that clumsy idiot.
What do we do with him?

32:54.764 --> 32:58.267
-Ugh! Why can't they control a single dog?
-Hey! Hey!

32:58.351 --> 33:01.020
You can't do that to trained dogs.

33:01.104 --> 33:02.438
Hey, let me handle it. Come on!

33:02.522 --> 33:04.691
Yeah, come here, boy! Come here!

33:08.903 --> 33:10.071
Don't let him escape.

33:11.406 --> 33:12.573
DAEJEON DAESEOK CHURCH

33:12.657 --> 33:15.410
SHARE YOUR LOVE WITH THOSE
WHO ARE VISUALLY IMPAIRED!

33:16.619 --> 33:18.329
Get down! Let's get him!

33:22.291 --> 33:23.501
-Get him.
-Huh? Hey, hey!

33:23.584 --> 33:25.628
How many cops
do you need to catch a dog?

33:25.712 --> 33:27.922
-He's trying to dig his way out.
-Stop it.

33:28.006 --> 33:30.133
-Get him!
-What's with this dog?

33:30.216 --> 33:32.760
-I told you…
-Grab the lead, tie him up.

33:32.844 --> 33:36.389
-Here, hook this up to the leash.
-Okay, right.

33:36.764 --> 33:38.433
-Stay.
-Here, put this on him.

33:38.516 --> 33:40.727
Sit. Good boy. Sit down.

33:41.310 --> 33:42.562
Ugh, seriously.

33:43.438 --> 33:44.647
INSURANCE PAYMENT RECORDS

33:44.731 --> 33:45.940
Hey.

33:46.524 --> 33:47.442
What?

33:48.234 --> 33:49.235
What is it?

33:50.445 --> 33:51.446
Tell me.

33:56.367 --> 33:58.494
Sir, you should come see this.

33:58.578 --> 34:00.288
What the heck is this now?

34:01.998 --> 34:03.249
Huh?

34:05.418 --> 34:06.711
Did forensics leave?

34:07.211 --> 34:10.631
They'd been missing for over
five years, so they were reported dead.

34:11.340 --> 34:12.925
As for Seon Yeo-ok,

34:13.009 --> 34:17.263
we couldn't find the cause of death
at the crime scene.

34:18.181 --> 34:20.600
Ah. There were some items of note,

34:21.184 --> 34:25.104
such as impact blood spatter, a moka
pot, a paper cup, and the milkman.

34:25.188 --> 34:28.441
Now, we are approaching this
as an active crime investigation,

34:28.524 --> 34:30.401
but we can't be sure quite yet.

34:30.902 --> 34:32.278
Also, uh…

34:32.987 --> 34:35.948
You can see here, um,
that the body has decomposed,

34:36.032 --> 34:38.451
and the entire wound area
is far from intact.

34:39.702 --> 34:43.247
So, uh, we're not sure what details
we'll get out of the autopsy.

34:43.331 --> 34:44.749
Is that so?

34:45.541 --> 34:47.001
And what about the bones?

34:49.420 --> 34:50.755
-Hey. The skeletons.
-Yes?

34:50.838 --> 34:52.006
-Th-the bones?
-Yes.

34:52.507 --> 34:53.674
Well, um,

34:54.175 --> 34:57.261
the two skeletons will
also get an autopsy tomorrow.

34:58.096 --> 34:59.889
-We'll wait for the results.
-I see.

35:01.349 --> 35:03.559
Let's skip
Team Four's briefing today.

35:03.643 --> 35:06.395
All right. Hmm? Anything to add?

35:25.373 --> 35:27.041
I learned something new.

35:29.460 --> 35:32.380
Humans can survive without any food
for four days.

35:33.631 --> 35:35.591
On the second day of starvation,

35:35.675 --> 35:38.469
you start crapping liquids
instead of solids.

35:38.553 --> 35:40.513
And you don't feel hungry anymore.

35:42.140 --> 35:44.976
Human life is resilient.

35:47.854 --> 35:48.771
No.

35:53.234 --> 35:54.819
Human life is easy to take.

36:10.001 --> 36:13.838
32 MISSED CALLS
BOSS (15), GYEONG-HWAN (13), MI-YEONG (3)

36:17.925 --> 36:22.096
It wasn't involuntary manslaughter,
accident, or self-defense.

36:22.597 --> 36:23.890
It was murder.

36:29.103 --> 36:32.273
So why is… no one coming to arrest me?

36:34.775 --> 36:38.905
Yes, we ran the paper cup, coffee beans,
and the fingerprints on the moka pot.

36:38.988 --> 36:41.282
We gave them a run-through on AFIS,

36:41.365 --> 36:44.118
but the ninhydrin reaction
showed nothing special.

36:45.786 --> 36:48.164
-N-ninhydrin?
-Mm, ninhydrin.

36:48.247 --> 36:50.374
-Sure, that. I know that. Yeah.
-Mm-hmm.

36:51.000 --> 36:54.253
And the coffee samples didn't show
anyone else's DNA either.

36:54.337 --> 36:56.964
-Mm.
-Everything else was covered with saliva.

36:57.548 --> 36:58.507
Huh?

36:59.008 --> 37:00.259
Yes, saliva.

37:00.343 --> 37:01.260
Dog drool.

37:02.553 --> 37:05.723
The dog must have licked all the surfaces
that had fingerprints on them.

37:05.806 --> 37:07.975
The door handles, the tables, the floor.

37:08.059 --> 37:09.644
There was dog drool everywhere.

37:10.686 --> 37:11.812
-Oh.
-Mm.

37:11.896 --> 37:12.772
Yeah.

37:13.689 --> 37:15.566
Did you find anything

37:15.650 --> 37:20.363
in those samples of dog poop
that I had submitted to be tested?

37:20.446 --> 37:21.614
The dog poop?

37:25.159 --> 37:27.578
Judging by your face,
I'd say you're innocent.

37:28.829 --> 37:30.581
Don't pick up
if Reporter Park calls.

37:30.665 --> 37:31.791
Yes, sir.

37:31.874 --> 37:33.000
What the heck is this?

37:33.084 --> 37:35.920
-Why a dog in the station? It's bad luck!
-What's with the dog?

37:36.003 --> 37:38.339
-To send a fecal sample to the NFS.
-Bring some salt!

37:38.422 --> 37:39.674
Salt? Yes, sir. Okay.

37:39.757 --> 37:42.176
Why didn't you just
send the dog there instead?

37:42.927 --> 37:45.763
Come on, go easy on him.
He's only trying to help.

37:46.514 --> 37:48.808
So? Did you find anything?

37:49.767 --> 37:52.353
-You think I would be here if we did?
-Jesus.

37:52.436 --> 37:54.188
Everything in there belonged to the girl.

37:54.272 --> 37:56.649
-Look after that.
-All that time, we didn't find shit.

37:57.316 --> 37:59.777
Are we sending the dog
to the district office?

37:59.860 --> 38:01.445
-What about the family?
-Uh…

38:01.529 --> 38:02.905
Don't even get me started.

38:02.989 --> 38:05.157
I talked to her family this afternoon.

38:05.241 --> 38:07.410
They asked why
we didn't have him killed already.

38:07.493 --> 38:10.121
They said that he might attack people.

38:11.914 --> 38:13.582
So they'll put him down?

38:15.751 --> 38:16.919
What a waste.

38:57.001 --> 39:00.212
Hey, I know you're home,
you crazy idiot!

39:00.296 --> 39:02.506
I saw the meter go up on the ground floor!

39:03.090 --> 39:05.134
Hello, ma'am. Hi.

39:05.676 --> 39:07.887
Right, so, I haven't
been able to reach Tang.

39:08.846 --> 39:11.640
He hasn't been coming to school,
and he's not taking any of my…

39:11.724 --> 39:13.392
I got you, you son of a…

39:13.476 --> 39:15.686
What's up with your face?
Is something wrong?

39:16.187 --> 39:17.897
Hey. Shut up.

39:20.024 --> 39:22.401
Uh, you little shit!
I came because I was worried.

39:22.485 --> 39:24.904
Oof!

39:24.987 --> 39:26.906
Do I look like a fucking pushover?

39:26.989 --> 39:28.532
You son of a bitch.

39:30.326 --> 39:32.244
For fuck's sake, come on.

39:32.328 --> 39:34.038
God, you're an idiot.

39:35.706 --> 39:37.291
Ah, you dumbass.

39:37.875 --> 39:39.251
You're the dumbass.

39:40.419 --> 39:42.755
You remember the tablet
you had in high school?

39:43.964 --> 39:47.009
I'm the one who stole it,
but you didn't even know, you jerk.

39:51.514 --> 39:52.973
You know what's funny?

39:54.642 --> 39:55.976
I knew it was you.

39:58.646 --> 40:00.439
We were both fucking losers.

40:01.982 --> 40:04.235
I didn't want to fuck up my life. Huh?

40:04.735 --> 40:06.529
So I pretended I didn't know.

40:06.612 --> 40:09.615
And then you started
being nice to me. Huh?

40:10.366 --> 40:11.409
Did you regret it?

40:12.660 --> 40:14.286
It was really confusing.

40:15.162 --> 40:17.665
I couldn't tell if you were
a good or bad guy.

40:20.376 --> 40:22.420
You thought I wouldn't know, asshole?

40:25.005 --> 40:27.049
Have fun rotting in the gutter forever.

40:28.050 --> 40:29.218
You shithead.

40:31.595 --> 40:32.930
And keep this.

40:35.015 --> 40:36.475
You fucking asshole.

40:37.351 --> 40:39.353
For fuck's sake. Jeez.

40:43.274 --> 40:45.860
So things are going
to get messy, all right,

40:45.943 --> 40:47.570
once news of this gets out.

40:48.112 --> 40:52.241
Do not let yourselves become distracted
by anything that happens.

40:52.324 --> 40:54.785
Just focus on the investigation.

40:54.869 --> 40:56.454
-Understood?
-Yes, sir.

40:58.038 --> 40:59.582
-Kang.
-Yes, sir.

41:00.166 --> 41:02.168
So tell me, how is the evidence so slim?

41:02.751 --> 41:05.796
-Proceed with caution…
-She brewed her coffee in a moka pot.

41:05.880 --> 41:09.884
But then she poured it into a paper cup
when she already has regular cups.

41:09.967 --> 41:11.760
-That's strange.
-This.

41:12.720 --> 41:15.097
It's murder. I'm absolutely sure of it.

41:15.973 --> 41:19.310
There was definitely
someone else with her that day.

41:19.810 --> 41:21.854
Someone she drank her coffee with.

41:22.938 --> 41:26.400
I think I could find something big
if I just dig more into this thing.

41:26.484 --> 41:30.112
-Why don't you talk to the boss, then?
-Trust me. I'm sure about this…

41:30.196 --> 41:31.238
'Cause there's no proof.

41:31.322 --> 41:33.699
-You still talking to that shaman?
-Well…

41:39.246 --> 41:40.498
All right, wake up.

41:41.832 --> 41:44.376
Why don't you just
sleep right on the floor, huh?

41:46.295 --> 41:48.422
Uh, what am I lookin' at?

41:48.506 --> 41:50.633
Well, it should've been
decided earlier, but…

41:52.760 --> 41:54.970
…there was a whole argument
about who was going to do it.

41:55.054 --> 41:56.764
And, well, we lost.

41:56.847 --> 42:00.351
Take that document with you,
the dog too, and they'll take care of it.

42:00.851 --> 42:03.229
You can just use the van.
It's open 24 hours.

42:03.312 --> 42:04.897
Mm. So he's getting put down.

42:06.565 --> 42:08.901
Hey, uh, I gotta take him?

42:08.984 --> 42:11.070
You're the only one here right now.

42:12.780 --> 42:15.157
Why'd we even bring him
here in the first place?

42:15.241 --> 42:16.492
Catch!

42:23.040 --> 42:24.833
You're open 24 hours, right?

42:25.709 --> 42:28.003
Oh, uh, can I get there a bit later?

42:29.338 --> 42:31.924
Uh, around 30 minutes, I guess?

42:32.007 --> 42:34.176
Right. Okay, yeah, yeah.

42:34.718 --> 42:36.720
Okay, thank you very much. Okay.

42:37.638 --> 42:40.015
What's goin' on?
Why are you pullin' me so hard?

42:40.516 --> 42:43.269
It's like you're not listening…
Hey, what are you doin'?

42:43.352 --> 42:45.354
You can't just go in there!

42:45.437 --> 42:46.814
What's in there?

42:46.897 --> 42:49.191
You're making a racket. Come here.

42:49.275 --> 42:50.526
Come on.

43:06.333 --> 43:07.835
NINE UNREAD MESSAGES

43:07.918 --> 43:10.504
HELLO, MR. LEE TANG
THIS IS DETECTIVE LEE CHANG-TAEK

43:10.588 --> 43:13.632
MR. JUNG GANG-HYO FROM OS25
FILED A COMPLAINT AGAINST YOU

43:13.716 --> 43:15.092
PLEASE REPLY

43:22.182 --> 43:25.936
-Why talk about girls again?
-Ugh, for fuck's sake.

43:26.020 --> 43:28.397
You always talk about girls
when you're drunk.

43:28.480 --> 43:29.607
Hey, hold on.

43:30.232 --> 43:32.484
Isn't that fucker the cop from last time?

43:32.568 --> 43:33.986
-Right?
-Huh?

43:34.778 --> 43:36.530
Man, I'll fucking gut that little bitch.

43:36.614 --> 43:37.948
-That bitch-ass cop.
-Hey.

43:38.032 --> 43:41.285
-I'll do it. I swear, man.
-Mess with a cop and you'll get gutted.

43:41.785 --> 43:44.580
The fuck you talking about, dumbass?
We could take him.

43:44.663 --> 43:45.914
-I'll do it.
-You stupid fucker.

43:45.998 --> 43:48.792
You don't think I remember
you pissing yourself in front of a cop?

43:48.876 --> 43:50.711
-I'll fuck him up.
-You'll fuck him up?

43:50.794 --> 43:52.296
Do it.

43:52.379 --> 43:53.589
-Hey, hey, hey!
-Shit.

43:53.672 --> 43:56.800
I fucking knew you couldn't do it.
Hey, hey, hey!

43:57.509 --> 43:59.511
Hey, hey, hey. Let's just go, man.

43:59.595 --> 44:02.139
Remember the asshole
who stuck a piece of gum in your hair?

44:02.222 --> 44:04.016
-With the beard?
-They're fucking pigs.

44:04.099 --> 44:06.727
You're a useless asshole.
Let's go fuck that guy up.

44:07.227 --> 44:08.562
Come on. Let's just go.

44:11.023 --> 44:13.859
What are you wagging your tail for
when you're gonna die?

44:15.235 --> 44:17.237
-Keep going'.
-Yo.

44:17.321 --> 44:19.281
-Hey, wait.
-Fuck you!

44:20.449 --> 44:21.784
You motherfucker!

44:21.867 --> 44:23.786
You shit. You fucking pig.

44:24.286 --> 44:25.704
What the fuck?

44:27.373 --> 44:29.458
That fucking idiot. We're fucked!

44:59.530 --> 45:03.200
DECEASED, BLIND WOMAN IN DAEJEON
FOUND TO HAVE MURDERED HER OWN PARENTS

45:07.454 --> 45:09.081
I learned one more thing.

45:11.458 --> 45:13.502
I realized the people I killed

45:13.585 --> 45:15.129
had deserved to die.

45:17.172 --> 45:18.215
Fuck me.

45:18.882 --> 45:20.426
I murdered two people,

45:21.552 --> 45:23.053
but there's no evidence.

45:26.807 --> 45:29.643
I guess I won the lottery.

45:35.107 --> 45:38.026
-Fuck, aren't we in trouble for real?
-Why?

45:38.110 --> 45:40.112
I might be an accomplice in this.

45:40.195 --> 45:42.906
-Hell yeah. Buy one, get one, bro.
-Ah, shit, man.

45:43.490 --> 45:46.535
Your parents will pay and settle this,
right? Won't they?

45:46.618 --> 45:47.995
-Right?
-I don't know. I don't know.

45:48.078 --> 45:48.996
-Jae-jun?
-Stop it.

45:49.079 --> 45:50.831
-Uh, they will, though, right?
-Cut it out.

45:50.914 --> 45:54.001
-Okay. They'll take care of it, though?
-I don't fucking know!

45:54.501 --> 45:57.087
-They have to.
-Mom'll kill me if I get in trouble.

45:57.171 --> 45:58.297
Let's go to yours.

45:58.839 --> 46:01.049
-I already told you my mom's there.
-Oh?

46:01.133 --> 46:03.093
Let's just go to the sauna, you idiot.

46:03.719 --> 46:05.554
Stop giving me shit, asshole.

46:06.096 --> 46:08.515
I'm sorry, all right?
I'm fucking sorry for everything.

46:08.599 --> 46:10.642
-Let's just go to the sauna.
-Cigarette.

46:12.144 --> 46:13.187
Huh?

46:13.270 --> 46:14.646
-Fuck. Fucking hell.
-Come on.

46:14.730 --> 46:16.148
I must have dropped them.

46:16.690 --> 46:19.151
-Cut the bullshit, dumbass.
-I'm serious, you idiot.

46:19.693 --> 46:21.236
Don't have 'em.

46:21.904 --> 46:26.074
-Fuck's sake. It wasn't easy to get them.
-We should've taken his fucking wallet.

46:26.158 --> 46:28.619
He ain't shit.
He's soaked in blood right now.

46:29.161 --> 46:31.705
-Hold on, come here. Jae-jun.
-Huh?

46:32.539 --> 46:33.999
On your left down the street.

46:34.500 --> 46:36.335
That skinny bastard there…
Wait, come back.

46:36.418 --> 46:38.796
-What about him?
-Should we rob him?

46:38.879 --> 46:41.089
-Ah! At it again, huh?
-Let's do it.

46:41.173 --> 46:42.883
-Want me to show you?
-Let me.

46:42.966 --> 46:44.343
-I'll do it.
-Move.

46:44.426 --> 46:46.094
-You got him?
-Don't be like that.

46:46.178 --> 46:47.971
-Fine.
-I know you've never done this.

46:48.055 --> 46:50.140
Fine, then show me. Hey, dude!

46:50.849 --> 46:53.018
Bro! Hello?

46:53.769 --> 46:54.645
Yo!

46:56.271 --> 46:58.148
The hell, man? We're talkin' to you. Hey.

46:59.858 --> 47:02.402
Jeez, you fuckin' reek of booze, bro.

47:27.427 --> 47:29.137
Come here!

48:05.549 --> 48:06.717
Hmm.

48:21.523 --> 48:22.691
Huh?

48:56.725 --> 48:59.311
REACH OUT IF YOU NEED HELP
TELEGRAM: T.ME/ONLYFORHEROES
